# issues/fixed/thread-join-was-re-callable-and-handles-leaked.md: a second
# `Thread.join` reached pthread_join on an already-joined thread (undefined
# behaviour; a closed HANDLE on Windows). It is now a panic naming the call.
# The program compiles cleanly and PANICS at run time; `build run` propagates
# that as a non-zero rc. The message rides stderr with build chatter and ends
# in a machine-specific `(at file:///…)`, so stdout keeps only the substring.
stdout_keep_match=Thread\.join: this thread was already joined
timeout=300
